    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 657,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "LGBT culture in Paris\nLGBT culture in France is centred on Paris , the capital city , where there is an active LGBT community . In the 1990s , 46 % of France 's gay men lived in Paris . As of 2004 , Paris had 140 LGBT bars , clubs , hotels , restaurants , shops , and other commercial businesses . Florence Tamagne , author of `` Paris : ` Resting on its Laurels ' ? '' , wrote that there is a `` Gait\u00e9 parisienne '' ; she added that Paris `` competes with Berlin for the title of LGBT capital of Europe , and ranks only second behind New York for the title of LGBT capital of the world . '' It has France 's only gayborhoods that are officially organized ."
     }
    ],
